"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Dockerfile.reviewbot:22 'python:3.12-slim is multi-arch and resolves to arm64 on the t4g (Graviton) box'","Dockerfile.reviewbot:51-54 the existing gitleaks installer maps both arm64->arm64 and amd64->x64, i.e. the image is built on arm64","Context names infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:43-71 as the runtime prerequisite the plan must satisfy","Plan Approach: 'validates the manifest's platform against its Docker build target ... before installing either scanner' — an amd64-only manifest fails this check on an arm64 build"],"finding":"The plan pins the scanner manifest to linux/amd64 ONLY and makes the Docker build path validate+consume that platform entry before provisioning, but the review-bot image it must satisfy is built for arm64 on the deployment target — so the platform self-check would fail the very image build the plan sets out to fix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9486ea37cf24fbb6","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / AC line 1 ('The checked-in scanner manifest names linux/amd64; the Docker build path ... validate and consume that same platform entry before provisioning')","norm_id":"n193451085b33f77b","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Building the review-bot image on the Graviton/t4g box: the amd64-only manifest fails the platform self-check and no scanner is installed, leaving the WS5 detectors fail-closed exactly as today","CI (linux x64) passes but the deployed arm64 image cannot provision, so mirror/Verified and deployment diverge"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["5 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Document a rollback/back-out procedure (e.g. bump-to-new-pin or mirrored-asset fallback) for a Gitleaks pinned-asset 404, since the plan re-adopts pinning despite the prior 404 concern.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.601,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the reproducibility and integrity benefit now outweighs the earlier pinned-version-404 concern'","AC2 pins 'one published Linux/amd64 release asset URL, version, and SHA-256'","No back-out plan stated if the pinned asset becomes unavailable"],"finding":"The plan pins Gitleaks to a specific published release asset URL while explicitly noting the earlier pinned-version-404 concern, but provides no rollback/back-out path if that pinned asset later 404s or is retracted — reintroducing the exact prior failure mode with no reversibility mechanism.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1b482184cc77b466","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('This deliberately supersedes...' paragraph) / AC2","norm_id":"n3ca5c75cb52866c3","priority":0.099,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Gitleaks retracts or moves the pinned release asset; provisioning hard-fails and Verified cannot vote"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add to docs/security.md the recovery step when a pinned Gitleaks asset 404s (bump manifest to a still-available release and its checksum, or point at an internal mirror), and note this in the Approach as the accepted mitigation for the reintroduced pinning risk.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State explicitly that the nine integration contracts still skip gracefully on non-linux/amd64 client shapes (macOS/Windows workstations, library use) and only run where the linux/amd64 scanners are provisioned, so the pin does not break the default suite off-platform.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.801,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: manifest 'names linux/amd64'; helper 'validates the manifest's platform against its Docker build target or CI runner before installing'","Plan Context: 'Nine real scanner integration tests skip when binaries are absent'","Gitleaks asset and Semgrep pip wheels are pinned to linux/amd64, not installable on macOS/Windows"],"finding":"The manifest is linux/amd64-only and the plan requires the nine real integration contracts to run with valid pinned inputs, but it never states what those contracts do on a non-linux/amd64 client shape (a macOS/Windows developer workstation, or the harness run as a library on such a host). Today they skip when binaries are absent; the plan is silent on whether that graceful-skip behavior is preserved off linux/amd64.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3eab707c6244883c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Acceptance Criteria line 5 ('passes the nine real Semgrep/Gitleaks integration contracts')","norm_id":"nf7387138c9132c22","priority":0.099,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["macOS developer workstation running the default test suite: if the nine contracts no longer skip when the linux/amd64-only scanners are absent, the suite errors/fails on a supported shape","Harness-as-library consumer on a non-linux host: same tests cannot provision the pinned scanners"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add an acceptance line: the nine contracts run when the pinned linux/amd64 scanners are present (Verified lane / review-bot image) and skip-with-reason elsewhere, preserving today's skip-when-absent behavior on unsupported platforms.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the exact source of the pinned Gitleaks SHA-256 (published `*_checksums.txt` release asset vs. maintainer-computed at pin time) and confirm it exists for the targeted release, so the digest-verification step and bad-SHA test are grounded.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7075,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'its pinned version, published per-release Linux/amd64 asset URL, and that tarball's SHA-256. The installer must verify the digest before extraction.'","AC2: 'The Gitleaks entry pins one published Linux/amd64 release asset URL, version, and SHA-256'","The Dockerfile confirms the asset URL surface (`gitleaks_${ver}_linux_x64.tar.gz`) is real/in-use, but the checksum SOURCE is a new asserted capability — UNVERIFIED from repo.","ANTI-FP: the asset URL itself is Verified (already used at Dockerfile.reviewbot:59); only the checksum-provenance claim is unverified."],"finding":"The plan asserts Gitleaks publishes a per-release SHA-256 checksum it can pin and verify before extraction, but never names where that checksum is obtained (e.g. a per-release `*_checksums.txt` asset vs. computing it locally at pin-time). The digest-verification step and the 'bad Gitleaks SHA-256 fails' acceptance test depend on this external capability, which is not verifiable from the repo.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdefc9c6a6e16a874","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / AC2 (\"pins one published Linux/amd64 release asset URL, version, and SHA-256\")","norm_id":"n21bba46a834603ea","priority":0.1925,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The pinned Gitleaks release does not ship a published checksum, forcing a local-compute pin the plan didn't design for","Checksum-asset naming differs across releases, breaking the version-bump procedure"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.35,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"insufficient","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibili